[
    {
        "content": "<p>In the comments of the PR <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39517\">#39517</a>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"669043\">@Yongxi Lin (Aaron)</span> and I discussed the possibility of providing a more general version of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MeasureTheory.TendstoInMeasure#doc\">docs#MeasureTheory.TendstoInMeasure</a>, which currently has the following definition:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MeasureTheory</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TendstoInMeasure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">EDist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MeasurableSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">μ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Measure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Filter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tendsto</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">μ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">edist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">})</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">𝓝</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>One could argue that a more general definition should be given in terms of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=UniformSpace#doc\">docs#UniformSpace</a>. The following definition, (provided by <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"669043\">@Yongxi Lin (Aaron)</span>) seems like a very natural generalization.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MeasureTheory</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TendstoInMeasure'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">UniformSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MeasurableSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">μ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Measure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Filter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">uniformity</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tendsto</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">μ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∉</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">})</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">𝓝</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>A potential benefit of this definition is that <code>UniformSpace</code> instances are in some sense more canonical than <code>EDist</code>. Also, unlike <code>EDist</code> (which can be an arbitrary function), a <code>UniformSpace</code> instance is naturally connected to a topology on <code>E</code>.</p>\n<p>I would be interested to hear the opinion of people familiar with the measure theory part of mathlib. Are there any potential issues with the new definition? Would such a generization be desired/worthwhile?</p>",
        "id": 597331971,
        "sender_full_name": "Joris van Winden",
        "timestamp": 1779562624
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Do you have a specific application in mind? Note that this new definition would not apply to <code>ENNReal</code>-valued functions (this space has an edist, but it is not an emetric space as the topology and the uniform structure don't come from the edist).</p>",
        "id": 597334750,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1779564969
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I did not have a concrete application in mind, and only propose this because it seems like the right level of generality.</p>\n<p>Regarding <code>ENNReal</code>, since it is not a <code>PseudoEMetricSpace</code>, many useful theorems about <code>TendstoInMeasure</code> already don't apply. Do you think <code>ENNReal</code>-valued functions are important to include?</p>",
        "id": 597335486,
        "sender_full_name": "Joris van Winden",
        "timestamp": 1779565589
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't know if they are important to include, it really depends on the applications. Finding the best level of generality is kind of a sweet spot: you want all the interesting applications to be possible, but you don't want to overgeneralize as it makes things harder to apply for practitioners of the area. Here, if we you don't have applications where the generality is needed, I'd say we should probably stick with the current definition -- but I'm definitely ready to change my mind the day a relevant application shows up!</p>",
        "id": 597336466,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1779566317
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Currently there does not even seem to be an <code>EDist</code> instance on <code>ENNReal</code> or <code>EReal</code>. </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EDist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EReal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fails</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EDist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ENNReal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fails</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 597336649,
        "sender_full_name": "Joris van Winden",
        "timestamp": 1779566453
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1010614\">Joris van Winden</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/generalization.20of.20.60TendstoInMeasure.60.3F/near/597336649\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Currently there does not even seem to be an <code>EDist</code> instance on <code>ENNReal</code> or <code>EReal</code>. </p>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EDist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EReal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fails</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EDist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ENNReal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fails</span>\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This is related to <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"287929\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/EMetricSpace.20is.20broken/with/597027863\">#mathlib4 &gt; EMetricSpace is broken</a></p>",
        "id": 597336792,
        "sender_full_name": "Yongxi Lin (Aaron)",
        "timestamp": 1779566558
